# s1_response_stream_v2 (PUMA): pickle the RunReturn response directly into the 10 MiB gRPC pieces.
#
# measured   peak   7,320,212 -> 6,410,776 kB   = -909,436 kB, -12.42%, factor 1.142x
#            wall         357 -> 362 s          = +1.4%, inside this step's own 2.5% spread
#            runs   3 replicates, spread 0.503% (baseline 0.882%)
# choice     s0_default peak:
#              4.89 GiB  75.6%  std::vector<pybind11::bytes>::emplace_back<std::string>  skipped
#              1.05 GiB  16.2%  _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault <- _PyBytes_Resize              <- this step
#              0.45 GiB   6.5%  _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault <- PyBytes_FromStringAndSize
#
# object_attacked: _PyBytes_Resize
# object_skipped: pybind11::bytes
# pool_attacked: host
# cost_class: free
#
# skip       depth probes p_pmdepth5/8/11: frame above emplace_back is inside libspu.so (spu==0.9.5
#            wheel, impl/puma.def); a fix means building SPU from source (replaces the measured
#            program). Peaks of the probes within 0.55%. off-path-runs/p_census/RESULT.md.
# object     fast census (impl/snni_fast_census.py, bytes >= 64 MiB, 98.6% of the peak):
#              375,054,672 B  frame distributed_impl.py:RunReturn:298 response
#              375,054,672 B  frame distributed_impl.py:RunReturn:298 response
#              375,054,672 B  dict
#              1,125,164,016 B against the recorder's 1,125,175,296 B row (0.001%)
#            three concurrent RunReturn calls, each holding a complete response.
# source     /opt/puma/examples/python/utils/distributed_impl.py, SPU commit 02ac612d:
#              result = fn(self, *args, **kwargs)                     # the SPU computation
#              response = cloudpickle.dumps(result)                   # ONE buffer, the whole result
#              for split in split_message(response):                  # ... cut into 10 MiB and yielded
#                  yield distributed_pb2.RunResponse(data=split)
# lever      CloudPickler writes into a sink cutting at RPC.CHUNK_SIZE; chunks pass through a bounded
#            queue (2 chunks = 20 MiB) from one worker thread to the generator.
# free       intermediate that never had to exist whole; no recompute, reload, extra round or order
#            change; byte stream to gRPC unchanged.
# checks     in image: CloudPickler(f).dump byte-identical to dumps (cloudpickle 3.1.2); identical
#            bytes and chunk count for a small object, a 250 MB object and None; early generator
#            close does not deadlock.
# gate       T2, tolerance 1.4e-2 absolute:
#              s0 against itself   2.560e-03  4.307e-03  5.180e-03
#              this step vs s0     2.064e-03 ... 5.703e-03 over three runs
#
# ============================================================================================
# v1 (off-path/s1_response_stream/WHY.md): replaced only the send loop and kept
# `response = cloudpickle.dumps(result)`, so the result was pickled twice; peak +3%, row unchanged.
# Its guard checked `payload`. v2 replaces the whole try/except/send block and refuses to write
# unless `response` is gone from the success path. Detected by the fast census.
